list) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Look up SMILES for multiple chemical names.\"\"\"\n    results = {}\n    for name in names:\n        try:\n            compounds = pcp.get_compounds(name, 'name')\n            if compounds:\n                results[name] = compounds[0].canonical_smiles\n        except Exception:\n            results[name] = None\n    return results\n```\n\n## Error Handling\n\n- Network errors: PubChem API requires internet access\n- Not found: `get_compounds` returns empty list for unknown chemicals\n- Rate limiting: PubChem may throttle excessive requests; add delays for large batches\n\n## Notes\n\n- The canonical SMILES from PubChem is standardized and suitable for fingerprint generation\n- `isomeric_smiles` preserves stereochemistry (important for chiral molecules)\n- For best results, use the most common name or IUPAC name\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2f62daf0-13cb-419b-bd6a-d55f71bd255e"}
{"parentUuid":"dc13c690-9e58-4a17-9ba6-4a5150dc6f61","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"90d3add8-3278-4b30-9f60-3448d6331c87","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"jaunty-sauteeing-moonbeam","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_017bVRpqDoGBXuweadvYQ3zz","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /root/environment/skills/rdkit-morgan-fingerprints.md"}]},"uuid":"da284601-0e03-4efb-8534-2782917cc44c","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:53:52.625Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/root/environment/skills/rdkit-morgan-fingerprints.md","content":"# RDKit: Morgan Fingerprints and Tanimoto Similarity\n\n## Overview\nRDKit is a cheminformatics toolkit that provides molecular fingerprint generation and similarity computation. Morgan fingerprints (circular fingerprints, similar to ECFP) are widely used for molecular similarity.\n\n## Installation\n```bash\npip install rdkit\n```\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### Morgan Fingerprints\nMorgan fingerprints are circular fingerprints that encode molecular substructure information. They are parameterized by:\n- **radius**: The number of bonds to consider around each atom (radius=2 ≈ ECFP4)\n- **nBits**: The length of the bit vector (default 2048)\n- **useChirality**: Whether to include stereochemistry information\n\n### Tanimoto Similarity\nTanimoto coefficient (Jaccard index for bit vectors):\n`T(A,B) = |A ∩ B| / |A ∪ B|`\nRange: [0, 1], where 1 = identical fingerprints.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Generate Morgan Fingerprint\n\n```python\nfrom rdkit import Chem\nfrom rdkit.Chem import AllChem, DataStructs\n\ndef get_morgan_fingerprint(smiles: str, radius: int = 2, n_bits: int = 2048, use_chirality: bool = True):\n    \"\"\"Generate Morgan fingerprint from SMILES string.\"\"\"\n    mol = Chem.MolFromSmiles(smiles)\n    if mol is None:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid SMILES: {smiles}\")\n    return AllChem.GetMorganFingerprintAsBitVect(\n        mol, radius=radius, nBits=n_bits, useChirality=use_chirality\n    )\n```\n\n### Compute Tanimoto Similarity\n\n```python\ndef tanimoto_similarity(fp1, fp2) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Compute Tanimoto similarity between two fingerprints.\"\"\"\n    return DataStructs.TanimotoSimilarity(fp1, fp2)\n```\n\n### Bulk Similarity Computation\n\n```python\ndef bulk_tanimoto_similarity(target_fp, fp_list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Compute Tanimoto similarity between a target and a list of fingerprints.\"\"\"\n    return DataStructs.BulkTanimotoSimilarity(target_fp, fp_list)\n```\n\n### Full Pipeline Example\n\n```python\nfrom rdkit import Chem\nfrom rdkit.Chem import AllChem, DataStructs\n\n# Convert SMILES to molecule\nmol1 = Chem.MolFromSmiles(\"CC(=O)Oc1ccccc1C(=O)O\")  # Aspirin\nmol2 = Chem.MolFromSmiles(\"CC(=O)O\")  # Acetic acid\n\n# Generate Morgan fingerprints (radius=2, with chirality)\nfp1 = AllChem.GetMorganFingerprintAsBitVect(mol1, radius=2, nBits=2048, useChirality=True)\nfp2 = AllChem.GetMorganFingerprintAsBitVect(mol2, radius=2, nBits=2048, useChirality=True)\n\n# Compute Tanimoto similarity\nsimilarity = DataStructs.TanimotoSimilarity(fp1, fp2)\nprint(f\"Tanimoto similarity: {similarity:.4f}\")\n```\n\n## Important Notes\n\n- `Chem.MolFromSmiles()` returns `None` for invalid SMILES - always check\n- `radius=2` is equivalent to ECFP4 (diameter 4)\n- `useChirality=True` makes the fingerprint sensitive to stereochemistry\n- `nBits=2048` is the standard bit vector length\n- `BulkTanimotoSimilarity` is more efficient than computing similarities one by one\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dc13c690-9e58-4a17-9ba6-4a5150dc6f61"}
{"parentUuid":"4d423af1-7b5e-4910-960a-6ca429ccdeea","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"90d3add8-3278-4b30-9f60-3448d6331c87","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"jaunty-sauteeing-moonbeam","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01GH7vjBGgtFFsinWKE1tA9R","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /root/environment/skills/pdf-text-extraction-python.md"}]},"uuid":"89de3b44-4e83-4bae-b5e7-c5d01f714bdd","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:53:52.678Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/root/environment/skills/pdf-text-extraction-python.md","content":"# PDF Text Extraction in Python\n\n## Overview\nMultiple libraries can extract text from PDF files in Python. Common options include pdfplumber, pypdf, and pdfminer.six.\n\n## Libraries\n\n### pdfplumber (Recommended for structured text)\n```bash\npip install pdfplumber\n```\n\n```python\nimport pdfplumber\n\ndef extract_text_from_pdf(filepath: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Extract all text from a PDF file.\"\"\"\n    text = \"\"\n    with pdfplumber.open(filepath) as pdf:\n        for page in pdf.pages:\n            page_text = page.extract_text()\n            if page_text:\n                text += page_text + \"\\n\"\n    return text\n```\n\n### pypdf\n```bash\npip install pypdf\n```\n\n```python\nfrom pypdf import PdfReader\n\ndef extract_text_from_pdf(filepath: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Extract all text from a PDF file.\"\"\"\n    reader = PdfReader(filepath)\n    text = \"\"\n    for page in reader.pages:\n        text += page.extract_text() + \"\\n\"\n    return text\n```\n\n## Parsing Chemical Names from Extracted Text\n\n```python\ndef parse_molecule_names(text: str) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Parse molecule names from extracted PDF text (one per line).\"\"\"\n    names = []\n    for line in text.strip().split('\\n'):\n        line = line.strip()\n        if line:  # skip empty lines\n            names.append(line)\n    return names\n```\n\n## Notes\n- pdfplumber handles multi-column layouts better than pypdf\n- For simple text-only PDFs, both work well\n- Always strip whitespace and filter empty lines when parsing line-based data\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4d423af1-7b5e-4910-960a-6ca429ccdeea"}
{"parentUuid":"4abcda2b-958d-4327-944d-7981ecc253d4","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"90d3add8-3278-4b30-9f60-3448d6331c87","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"jaunty-sauteeing-moonbeam","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01NseanBFFFy35V2Hkj9ds4k","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /root/environment/skills/tanimoto-similarity-ranking.md"}]},"uuid":"b1a59f66-84be-48ac-b9b8-d06aff34aaf1","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:53:52.696Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/root/environment/skills/tanimoto-similarity-ranking.md","content":"# Tanimoto Similarity Ranking for Molecules\n\n## Overview\nThis skill covers the complete pipeline for ranking molecules by similarity to a target molecule using Morgan fingerprints and Tanimoto similarity.\n\n## Complete Pipeline\n\n### 1. Load molecule pool from file (PDF)\n```python\nimport pdfplumber\n\ndef load_molecules_from_pdf(filepath: str) -> list:\n    text = \"\"\n    with pdfplumber.open(filepath) as pdf:\n        for page in pdf.pages:\n            page_text = page.extract_text()\n            if page_text:\n                text += page_text + \"\\n\"\n    return [line.strip() for line in text.split('\\n') if line.strip()]\n```\n\n### 2. Convert names to SMILES via PubChem\n```python\nimport pubchempy as pcp\n\ndef name_to_smiles(name: str) -> str:\n    compounds = pcp.get_compounds(name, 'name')\n    if compounds:\n        return compounds[0].canonical_smiles\n    return None\n```\n\n### 3. Generate fingerprints and compute similarity\n```python\nfrom rdkit import Chem\nfrom rdkit.Chem import AllChem, DataStructs\n\ndef compute_similarity(target_smiles: str, pool_smiles: list, radius=2, use_chirality=True):\n    target_mol = Chem.MolFromSmiles(target_smiles)\n    target_fp = AllChem.GetMorganFingerprintAsBitVect(\n        target_mol, radius=radius, nBits=2048, useChirality=use_chirality\n    )\n\n    similarities = []\n    for smiles in pool_smiles:\n        mol = Chem.MolFromSmiles(smiles)\n        if mol:\n            fp = AllChem.GetMorganFingerprintAsBitVect(\n                mol, radius=radius, nBits=2048, useChirality=use_chirality\n            )\n            sim = DataStructs.TanimotoSimilarity(target_fp, fp)\n            similarities.append(sim)\n        else:\n            similarities.append(0.0)\n    return similarities\n```\n\n### 4. Rank and return top-k\n```python\ndef get_topk(names: list, similarities: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Return top-k molecules sorted by similarity (desc), then alphabetically for ties.\"\"\"\n    paired = list(zip(names, similarities))\n    # Sort by similarity descending, then by name ascending for ties\n    paired.sort(key=lambda x: (-x[1], x[0]))\n    return [name for name, _ in paired[:k]]\n```\n\n## Sorting Rules\n- **Primary**: Descending similarity score\n- **Secondary (tie-breaking)**: Alphabetical order (ascending) by molecule name\n\n## Edge Cases\n- Target molecule may or may not be in the pool\n- Some names might not resolve in PubChem\n- Invalid SMILES should be handled gracefully\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4abcda2b-958d-4327-944d-7981ecc253d4"}
